        "text": "Fever, with burning, retching, drowsiness and delirium supervenes and ultimately the patient loses all conscious-ness. The remedy consists in the administration of an anti-toxic medicine known as Mahagada, as snuffs, potions and unguents, etc. A bite by an Indrayudha usually proves fatal. Venomous leeches, as well as cures for their bites, have thus been described. The non-venomous species include Kapilas, Pingalas, Shankhamukhis, Musikas, Pundarimukhis and Saravikas.",
