        "text": "The Pundarimukhas are coloured like the IMudga pulse and are so called from the fact of the resemblance of their mouths to the full-blown lotus hhes TPimdarikas). The Saravikas have cold bodies marked with impress-ions like lotus leaves and measure eighteen fingers\nwidth in length, and they should be employed in sucking blood from the affected parts of lower animals. This exhausts the list of non-venomous leeches. The countries, such as Turkesthan (Yavana), the Deccan (Pandya), the tract of land traversed by the Ghaut mountains (Sahya), and Pautana (modem Mathura), are the natural habitats of these leeches.",
