        "sanskrit": "न च विकेशिकौषधे+अतिस्निग्धे+अतिरूक्षे विषमे वा कुर्वीत यस्मादतिस्नेहात् क्लेदो रौक्ष्याच्छेदो दुर्न्यासाह्रणवर्त्मावघर्षणमिति",
        "text": "A loose bandaging (Shithila-Vandha) should be the rule in the region of the eyes and locations of important joints or unions. An ulcer, brought about or characterised b) the symptoms of the deranged Pittam and occurring at a place where a tight bandaging is indicated, should be fastened with one of the Sama-Vandha class, and with a Shithila bandage where one of the Sama type would be indicated ; whereas it should not be bandaged at all in the event of a loose bandage (Shithila-Vandha) being indicated. The same rule should be observed in the case of an ulcer caused through a diseased or contami-nated state of the blood.",
