        "text": "It is a tonic and aphrodisiac, subdues the deranged Yayu and proves soothing to the deranged Pittam. The IVlahat Panchamula Croup:—\nThe one known as the great or the major group of five medicinal roots (Mahat-Pancha-Mula) consists of the roots of such trees as Vilva, Agnimantha, Tuntuka, Patala and Kashmari. Metrical Texts :— It is bitter in taste and subdues the deranged Kapham and Vatam.",
