        "text": "It is light (easily digestible) and appetising, and acquires a sub-sequent sweet taste in its reaction (Anurasa). The Dashamula Croup :— The two preceding groups in combination form the one techni-cally known as the Dasha-Mulam (the ten roots), which is possessed of the virtue of destroying the deranged Vata, Pittam and Kapham. It proves beneficial in cases of asthma and difficult respiration.",
