        "sanskrit": "भवति चात्र /",
        "text": "These .tastes, in groups of different combinations, number sixty-three in all ; as for example, fifteen, computed b)\" taking two at a time ; twenty, computed by taking three at a time ; fifteen, computed by taking four at a time ; six, computed by taking five at a time and six, being severally computed, thus making up an aggregate of sixty-three. Authoritative verse on the sub-ject : — The man, who gradually habituates him-self to the use of each of the six aforesaid tastes, enjo5''s a sort of immunity from their injurious action in the same manner as, a strong man, who makes him-self successively accustomed to the action of the three deranged humours of his bod)\", is not easily affected by their pathogenetic properties. Thus ends ihe forty-second Chapter of the Sutrasthinam in the Sushruta SamhitS, which treats of the specific properties of flavours.",
