        "text": "This disease is called Apatantrakah and is ascribed to the action of the enraged Vayu surcharged with the deranged Kaphani. 56.\nlYIanyastambha:— The local Vayu. agitated through such causes as sleep in the da- time, reclining with the neck on an uneven place or pillow, gazing upward for a considerable length of time, or looking aside in a contorted way, and enveloped in the deranged Kapham, gives rise to the disease known as Manya-stambha (wr- neck or torticollis). 57.",
