        "text": "Ch. CLXIXV. 4.\nnature. A sort of pricking, piercing pain (is experienced in the affected locality) which loses all sensibility to the touch. The type known as Audumbara is coloured and shaped like a ripe or mature Audumbara fruit and has its origin in the deranged Pittam. The t>'pc called Rishyajihva is rough and resembles the tongue of a Risha (Deer) in shape and colour.",
