        "text": "If the two diflTerent readings ITI \"< <?f%51'C betaken con-jointly into consideration we are impressed with the idea that in ancient 6o THE SUSriRUTA SAMHITA. CChap. VIII. India Cicsarean operations were very frequently undertaken in cases of puerperal eclampsia, where the molher had been in the deplorable condi-tion of a goat sufTeriny from cramps and convulsions as well as in cases of an accidental death not unlike that which fell to the lot of the poor molher of him in whose nnme the operation is called. q = goat\"in =\ndestroyer (Sec Monier William's Dictionary) hence a goat-destroyer = a tiger or wolf) or in cases where the presence of deformity in the parturient canal or of maUormalion of the foetus prevented the natural delivery of a living child.",
