        "text": "Seated on the heart it gives rise to an excruciating and piercing pain within its cavity and a drawing pain (Graha) extending all over the body (D. R. — cough). Seated in the Liver its characteristic indications are thirst and difficult breathing (D. R. — hic-cough) whereas a sort of unquen-chable thirst is the symptom which marks its seat on the Kloma. 16-17.",
