        "text": "The unexpelled blood is called Makkalla. Such an abscess, if not absorbed in the course of a week, is sure to suppurate. 20 - 21. Differentiating diagnosis of Gulma and Vidradhi :— Now I shall discuss the features which distinguish a Gulma (internal tumour; from a Vidradhi (internal abscess).",
