        "text": "A smashed condition of the fractured bone marks a case of the PicUoMtim kind which is often found to be marked by a great swelling. The case where the covering or skin of the bone (periosteum) is cast or splintered off is called the Asthi-chchalUtatn. The case where the completely broken or severed bone? are found to project through the local skin, is called Killda-bhagnam (compound).",
