        "text": "The case where a fragment of the fractured or broken bone is found to pierce into the bone and dig out the marrow, is called JVEljjaaugatam, (Impacted fracture). The case where the fractured bone droops or hangs down is called Ati-patitam. The case where the unloosened bone (from its position) is bent down in the form of an arch is called Vakram The case where only one articular extremity of the bone is severed is called Chhinnan.",
