        "text": "Memorable Verses :— A physician should cause the longings of a pregnant woman (Dauhrida)\nto be gratified inasmuch as such gratifications would alleviate the discomforts of gestation ; her desires being fulfilled ensure the birth of a strong, long-lived, and virtuous son. A non-fulfilment of her desires during pregnancy, proves injurious both to her child and her ownself. A non-gratification of any sensual enjoy-ment by its mother '.Dauhrida) during gestation tends to painfully affect the particular sense-organ of the child.",
