        "text": "Thus a total number of sixty-six bones is made up. (Hence) the total number of three hundred bones is made (with the grand total of the iliree foregoing totals). Thus the list of bones of a skeleton is described.\"\n(hips), and the fifth one is the Trika or triangular bone (the sacrum). There are thirty-six bones in one Parjsva (side), and the same number in the other ; thirty in the Prishtha (back), eight in the Urah (chest) ; and two more known as Akshaka (collar-bone).\n(Thus making one hundred and seventeen in all). 19.",
