        "text": "The bones, situated in the knee-joints, shoulders (Ansa-f), hips (Nitamvas), cheeks (Ganda palate, temples, and the cranium belong to the Kapfcla kind (flat bones). The teeth belong to the Rucliaka, class. The bones in the nose, ears, throat (trachea) and the socket of the eyes (Akshi-koshaf ) are called Tarana (cartilages) ; while those which are found in the palm (wrist), foot (ankle), sides back, chest and regions of the abdomen, belong to the Valaya (irregular or curved) class.",
