        "text": "A child unruffled by any of the above ways becomes healthy, cheerful and intelligent as it grows older. An infant should be guarded against any exposure to the rains, the sun, or the glare of lightning. He should not be placed uuder a tree or a creeper, in low lands, and in lonely houses or in their shades (cavesl ; and it should be protected from the malignant influences of evil stars and occult powers. 38. Metrical Texts : —A child should not be left (alone) in an unclean and unholy place, nor under the sky 232 THE SUSHRUTA SAMIIITA. [Chap. X.\n(uncovered place), nor over an undulating ground, nor should it be exposed to heat, storm, rain, dust, smoke and water.",
