        "text": "Now we shall discourse on the medical treatments of fractures and dislocations (Bhagnas). i. Metrical Texts :— A fracture or dislocation (Bhagna) occurring in a person of a Vatika tempera-ment, or of intemperate habits, or in one who is sparing in his diet, or is affected with such supervening disorders (as fever, tympanites, suppression of the stool and urine, &c.) is hard to cure. A fracture-patient must forego the use of salt, acid, pungent and alkaline substances and must live a life of strictest continence, avoid expo-sure to the sun and forego physical exercises and parchi-fying (devoid of oleaginous) articles of food.",
