        "text": "Diaphoretic measures should be applied according to the prescribed rules. In a case marked by an unusually aggravated condition of the Vayu, the patient should be made to stand neck-deep in a pit tolerably warmed or heated with burning husks, and cow-dung. As an alternative, Palas'a leaves should be strewn over a hot stone-slab or over a hot oven, after having sprinkled wine over them, and the patient should be laid full length upon these leaves, or fomentations should be made with Ves'avdrdy Kris'ara and Pdyasa. 24—25. An oil, cooked in combination with the expressed viz., the Vataghna drugs, Yava, Kola, Kulaltha and flesh. Others, again, mean by the term \"Pancha-varga\" the five parts, viz., leaf, fruit, flower, bark and root, of the Vataghna drugs mentioned in the sentence.",
