        "text": "Uru-Stambha :— The deranged Vayu, sur-charged with the local fat and Kapha gives rise to a swelling in the region of the thigh which is known as Ura-stambha ; others designate it as Adhya-Vata. This disease is marked by lassitude and an aching pain in the limbs, by the presence of fever, horripilation and somnolence and by a sensation of coldness, numbness, heaviness, and unsteadiness in the thighs, which seem foreign to the body.",
