        "text": "XII.\nit should be treated as a swelling in its unsuppurated stage. Medicated oils should be likewise employed for the purposes of healing (RopanaJ, etc. 8. A decoction of the drugs of the Aragvadhddi group should be used for the purpose of raising up (UtScidana)\nthe cavity of the incidental ulcer ; that of the S'ala-sdra'di group should be used for sprinkling purposes ; that of the drugs of the Pippalyddi gvow\" should be given as food and drinks. A pulverised compound o( Pdthd, Chitraka, S'drmgashtd, Kshudra, Vrihati, S'drivd Soma-valka Saptaparna, Aragvadka and Kutaja roots mixed with honey should be internally given to the patient.",
