        "sanskrit": "काकोलिवर्गस्य च शीतलानि पिबेत् कषायाणि सशर्कराणि/ द्राक्षारसेनेक्षुरसेन वा+अपि चूर्णं पिबेच्चापि हरीतकीनाम्",
        "text": "Hot plasters, prepared by pasting together the bark of the Madlnika (flower) tree, and of the Jambu Some read ''f - JTIiTl 'ia!\" and explain that the; decoclions of the Vilvadi and the Arkadi groups are to be taken for the purpose.\ntree, Arjuna tree, and Vetasa creeper. As an alter-native, hot plasters compounded of the roots of the Trina-s'unya (Ketaki), or Muchukunda mixed with sugar, should be constantly applied to the affected part.",
