        "text": "The refuse of another's dishes, as well as articles of food infested with flies, insects, etc. or possessed of an objectionable colour, taste, smell, touch or Some explain \"Jyotish\"' as a blaze 0.' fire and olhers explain it as stars.\nt The framers of the Ayurveda were aware of the fact that the human system is incapable of directly assimilating starchy substances without converting them into sugar, This has been emphasised in the Sutra-Sihana, where Sus'ruta insists that a food stuff, in order to be worthy of the epithet, must be Madhura (z e , of sweet flavour) and contain a large qnantity of proteid n>atter such as is found in milk, butter, meat, etc.— Ed.\n495 THE SUSIIRUTA SAMIIITA [Chap.",
