        "number": "128",
        "sanskrit": "उपदंशस्तथा वायोः कोपः शुक्रस्य च क्षयः/ उच्चारिते मूत्रिते च रेतसश्च विधारणे",
        "text": "Fatigue after coition should be re-moved by the enjoyment of a bath f, a cool breeze, or a It should be always borne in mind that God has iir.planted this desire in the mind of man and provided him with the necessary organic appendages only for the propagation of his species and not for the gratification of any diseased or morbid sexual propensity which is found nowhere else in Nature save and except in debauched human subjects and which lowers them even below the level of brutes.",
