        "sanskrit": "लाक्षाविडङ्गकल्केन तैलं पक्त्वा+अवचारयेत्/ स्विन्नां गोमयपिण्डेन प्रदिह्यात् परिलेहिके",
        "text": "S'ydmd and Arka pasted together (with cow's urine\nor with the pastes of Karanja-sQzd, Ingudi seed, Kutaja and Aragvadha (pasted with cow's urine). Mustard oil cooked with the admixture of all the foregoing drugs and with Markka, Nhnba-ca,Q.s and wax, proves effi-cacious as unguents (in such cases). 14-15-In cases where the ear-lobes are affected and have become either thin, or hard, an ointment should be applied to them in order respectively to increase their growth, or to soften them. 16.",
