        "text": "All these kinds of Soma secure for the user a mastery of the Gdyatri (and hence in the Vedas), and are known by the above auspicious names mentioned in the Vedas These are decrepitude, death, hunger, thirst, sleep, etc.\nt Here death may mean, according to some authorities, the death of tissues as well.\n% The whole of the hymns in the gih Book of the Rig-veda, besides a few in other places, are dedicated to the honour of Soma, but these twenty-four names do not occur there.",
