        "number": "15",
        "sanskrit": "रूक्षक्षतविषार्तानां वातपित्तविकारिणाम्/ हीनमेधास्मृतीनां च सर्पिःपानं प्रशस्यते",
        "text": "One is called the KeClinga and the The Kashaya-Paka Kalpa :— The bark, roots and leaves, etc., of medicinal drugs should be dried in the sun and taken in any of the aforesaid measures, should be cut in small pieces, or pounded, as the case may be, and soaked in a quantity of water\nweighing eight or sixteen times their combined weight.",
