        "text": "A purgative medicine should not be administered before the digestion of a meal previously taken, neither in the diseases due to an abuse of wine, nor in acute catarrh and acute fever or to a newly parturient woman and persons not previously treated with a Sneha (oil or GhritaX A mild purgative may, however, be adminis-tered (in cases of emergency) to a person of extremely Pitta-predominant temperament. Purgatives adminis-tered by ignorant physicians to persons who ought not to be purged (often) prove fatal. 19.",
