        "sanskrit": "या तु विरेचने गुदपरिकर्तिका तद्वमने कण्ठक्षणनं, यदधः परिस्रवणं स ऊर्ध्वभागे श्लेष्मप्रसेकः, या त्वधाः प्रवाहिका सा तूर्ध्वं शुष्कोद्गारा इति",
        "text": "The patient should in such a case f be made to speedily vomit the contents of his stomach, and the concomitant symptoms (such as fever, etc.'l should be treated with appropriate medicinal remedies (as in the case of their actual and respective attacks). Drugs efficacious in subduing the Doshas confined in the lower cavity (abdomen) of the body (Adhobhdga-hard) should be employed for purgative purposes with the admixture of Dallana recommends bolh Niruha and Snaihika Vastis in such cases.\nt This evidently refers to the case of an abuse of an emetic. Saitidhava, Kdnjika and cow's urine in cases of the retention of the stool, etc., due to an abuseof a purgative. Proper Asthapana and Anuvasana Vastis should be prescribed in consideration of the nature and intensity of the Doshas involved in the case.",
