        "sanskrit": "निरूहः शोधनो लेखी स्नैहिको बृंहणो मतः/ निरूहशोधितान्मार्गान् सम्यक् स्नेहो+अनुगच्छति/ अपेतसर्वदोषासु नाडीष्विव वहज्जलम्",
        "text": "As water will freely run through channels previously cleansed of all refuse matter, so does an Anu-vasana tend to cleanse the organism of all Doshas (morbific diatheses) and to increase the vitality of the organism. A Sneha-vasti should, therefore; be applied to a person previously purged of all Doshas by the application of a Niruha-vasti. 12. Both the Anuvdsana and the AsthapAna Vastis should be regarded as forbidden in cases of insanity, in the mental conditions of terror and grief, of a thirsty state of the body, of aversion to food and of indigestion, jaundice i (Pdndu), giddiness, delirium, epilepsy, vomiting, Kushtha, Meha, ascites, obe?ity, asthma, cough, dryness of the throat and oedema as well as in respect of a Kshata-Kshina patient and a pregnant woman in (and before) the third or the fourth month of her gestation, in the case of a person suffering from dulness of appetite, impatient and incapable of bearing the least pain as well as in respect of infants, old men and persons emaciated by a bodily distemper other than one due to Vayu 13.",
