        "text": "The strength and complexion of the patient suffer much by the application of an Anuvasana-vasti after he has taken a dry (Ruksha) meal containing no Sneha. A patient should, therefore, be first fed with a diet saturated with a moderate quantity of an oleaginous substance before being treated with an Anuvasana-vasti. The patient before being treated with an Anuvasana vasti should be fed with Mudga-soup \"j\", cow's milk and meat-essence to a quarter part X\nless than the quantity he can ordinarily take 16.\nt Dallana explains that the Mudga soup should be taken without being mixed with any Sneha. He further says that the patient should be given Mudga-soup, cow's milk and meat -essence in accordance with the aggravation of the deranged Kapha, Pitta and Vayu respectively. X Dallana, on the authority of the older Commentators explains that the patient should not be fed to his fill but only to three-fourths, half and one-fourth of what he can ordinarily take according to his digestive capacity. The mode of applying a Sneha-Vasti : — The body of the patient to be treated with an Anuvsana vast! should be first anointed (with a Sneha) and gently fomented with hot water. Then he should be advised to take his meal in the prescribed way and made to take a short walk.",
