        "text": "The patient may be given a light + meal or diet in the evening, in case he is possessed of a keen digestive capacity , subsequent to the digestion of a previous meal and (should he feel hungry) after the discharging of the injected Sneha. Tepid water boiled with Dhanydka It should be noted that the particle •'' \" in the text means that on the satisfactory action of an Anuvasana-Vasti, the injected S neha may come out with urine as well.\nt Dallana explains '' t \" to mean thirst. X \"Light\" means both light in quantity as well as in quality. Some commentators explain this couplet to mean that a patiant .of ordinary digestive capacity should be given a light food, whereas a patient of keen digestive capacity may take a full one.\nand S'linthi should be given hot to the patient on the (following I morning as it would sharpen his appetite and produce a fresh relish for food.",
