        "sanskrit": "त्र्यहं त्र्यहं परिहरेदेकैकं बस्तिमातुरः तृतीये तु परीहारे यथायोगं समाचरेत्",
        "text": "Intervals of three days should be allowed between two successive applications of a Vasti and the period of the third interval thus allowed, should be determined according to the require-ments of each case. 13, A patient suffering from an ulcer (Vrana) or recently treated with emulsive measures (Sneha-karma) or cleans-ing (emetics or purgatives) measures, or afflicted with any affection of the eyes or with fever attended with dysentery (Jvaratisara) resembles a vessel of unbaked clay fitted with oil, i.e. such a patient is greatly liable to the derangement of the Doshas. 14.",
