        "sanskrit": "मैथुनोपगमाद्घोरान् व्याधीनाप्नोति दुर्मतिः/ आक्षेपकं पक्षघातमङ्गप्रग्रहमेव च",
        "text": "Talking in a loud voice aggravates the Vdyu and is attended with such grave consequences as pain in the head, blindness, inertness, loss of the faculty of smell, dumbness, deafness, dislocation of the jaw-bones (Hanu-moksha), Adhi-mantha, facial paralysis, paralysis of the eye-balls (Netra-stambha), thirst, cough, insomnia, shak-ing of the teeth and similar other distempers (due to an aggravation of the Vdyu). 15 C.",
        "iast": "maithunopagamādghorān vyādhīnāpnoti durmatiḥ/ ākṣepakaṃ pakṣaghātamaṅgapragrahameva ca"
