        "text": "Metrical Text:— The processes of inhalation and fumigation have been briefly described above. Now I shall fully describe the processes of using medicinal snuffs (Nasya). 17. On Snuffs and Errhines:— The term \"Nasya\" (Snuff) is so called from the fact of its being composed of the powders of any drugs or of any Sneha (oleaginous substance\") cooked with such drug or drugs, to be stuffed into the nostrils. It may be broadly divided into two kinds, viz. : — Siro Virechana (errhines) and Snehana (contributor of oleaginous principles); and may, however, be further grouped under five specific heads, z; ,?. :— Nasya, Siro-Virechana, Pratimarsha (a medicated Sneha poured into the nostrils to be discharged into the mouth), Avapida (the expressed juice of any drug put into the nostrils in drops by pressing it with the palms then and there)\nand Pradhamana (a medicinal snuff blown into the nostrils with the help of a blowpipe).",
