        "sanskrit": "अवपीडस्तु शिरोविरेचनवदभिष्यण्णसर्पदष्टविसंज्ञेभ्यो दद्याच्छिरोचिरेचनद्रव्याणामन्यतममवपिष्यावपीड्य च, शर्करेक्षुरसक्षीरघृतमांसरसानामन्यतमं क्षीणानां शोणितपित्ते च विदध्यात्",
        "text": "Measures and remedies possessed of the virtue of subduing the deranged Kapha and Vayu should be (re-spectively) employed in cases of excessive and deficient applications of (an oleaginous) errhine (Nasya), while in the case of a proper and satisfactory application the patient should be made to snuff in a quantity of clarified butter on each alternate day or at an interval of two days for one, two or three weeks in succession or for any longer period as considered proper according to the exigency of the case.",
