        "text": "The four different modes of using snuff have thus been described in all of which oil may be used as not being hostile in its action as regards the seats of Kapha within the organism. 38. Kavala-graha : — Now we shall describe the process of using medicinal gargles (Kavala) which may be divided into four kinds, viz. : — The Snehi (oleaginous), Prasadi (soothing), Sodhi (purifying) and the Ropana (healing).",
