        "text": "Recipes of remedies in different cases : — An anti-venomous compound (Agada) con-sisting oi Kushtha, Chakra(T 2ig3.-Si), Vachd, Vtlva-roots, Pdthd, Suvarchikd, house-soot and the two kinds of Haridrd is efficacious in the case of a bite by a Trikan-taka insect. An Agada consisting of house -soot, i?(7;' ;\"', Chakra, Kushtha and the seeds of Palds'a destroys the poison of a Gala-goli insect. An Agada composed of Kumkuma, Tagara, S'igru, Padmaka and the two kinds of Rajani, pasted with water, proves curative in the case of a bite by a S'ata-padi (centipede). An Agada consist-ing of Mesha-s'ringi, Vachd, Pdthd, Nichula, Rohini, and Bdlaka is efficacious in all kinds of Manduka-poisoning. An Agada consisting of Vacha, As'va-gandhd, Ati-bald, Bald, Ati-guhd (Sala-parni) and AguJid ( Pris'ni-parni) nullifies the poison of a VisVambhara insect. An Agada consisting of S'irisha, Tagara, Kzcshtha, the two kinds of Haridrd, Afns'u-tnati and the two kinds of Sahd destroys the poison of an Ahinduka insect. Cooling measures should be adopted in the night time in the case of a Kandumaka-bite, since the poison which is aggravated by the sun's rays in the day does not prove amenable to any remedy, if applied at that time. An Agada consisting of Chakra, Kushtha and Apd-mdrga is efficacious in a case of Suka-vrinta-bite. As an alternative, the earth of a black ant-hill pasted with the expressed juice oi Bhrmga would prove efficacious in such cases. A plaster prepared with the earth of a black ant-hill and the urine of a cow proves curative in cases of bites of Hies, ants and mosquitoes. The treatment of a case of a bite by a Prati-suryaka is the same as that of a snake-bite."
